From 50c3665234dff32c0ac9bcb83ab6903fcd524b7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowOS <powos@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:56:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: a window that takes a full-screen game's
 focus opens in front of it, and a restored game that stops drawing is
 restored again

11-08 02:03 (bf-pacing play, Broforce): xdotool's XTEST made KWin start kwin_eis_prompter (Remote Control) with a
privileged activation token. The prompt became a web window of home under the game's full-screen layer - unseen,
unanswered ("shown 99601 ms after open") - while it held the focus: the game minimized itself, 0040 restored it and
made it active, and the restored game sometimes never drew again (window task 52: 0 commits for good, engine running).

1. A new window that takes the activation from a live full-screen task (another app's - a prompt, polkit, a portal
   dialog) is sent as "parent <id> <full-screen task>" before its "open": the app opens it as a task in front of the
   full-screen web window (WindowTasks overFull). Over a full-screen task, exportNew waits up to 400 ms for the
   activation a token gives after the map. A window that doesn't take the focus opens as before.
2. While such a window has the focus, the game's self-minimize is still undone but its focus is not taken back; when
   the window closes, the full-screen task gets the focus back (restored if minimized).
3. A full-screen window restored after its own minimize is watched for 20 s (from the restore or its focus again): one
   that has the focus and commits nothing for 3 s is minimized and restored again after 500 ms (Iconic, then Normal,
   then the focus, the order Wine acts on), twice at most. A hack (marked in the code): the recovery; the cause is in Wine's window-state
   handling of a restore right after its own iconify.

Decisions in anland_task_policy.h (test/task-policy-test.cpp).
